  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nDaytime temperatures will run around 5 degrees warmer than \nyesterday's as high pressure becomes established over the region. \nTemperatures will increase by another few degrees on Sunday, warming \nto around 5 to 10 degrees above climatological norms. These above \nnormal temperatures will persist through late next week, with many \nlow-elevation areas reaching 60 degrees multiple days. A couple of \nweak shortwaves are still expected to swing through Sunday and late \nMonday/early Tuesday. With precipitation largely remaining north of \nour CWA, the only impacts look to be a few degree loss on our \ndaytime temps Tuesday. There still remains uncertainty regarding the \nupper-level pattern come late next week/weekend with some solutions \nintroducing a trough late week while others maintain the ridge \nthrough late weekend. The National Blend introduces low-end PoPs in \nthe central mountains as early as Thursday night, becoming \nwidespread by Saturday.",
